turns.prompt:
This class simulates how a dynamic array such as a Python list grows: when it is full, it moves every item into a new block twice as large and counts the moved items. What does it print? What do the numbers tell you about the cost of a single append and of n appends?

class DynArray:
    def __init__(self):
        self.size, self.cap, self.copies = 0, 1, 0

    def append(self, x):
        if self.size == self.cap:
            self.copies += self.size  # move every item to a bigger block
            self.cap *= 2
        self.size += 1

for n in [16, 17, 1000]:
    arr = DynArray()
    for i in range(n):
        arr.append(i)
    print(n, arr.cap, arr.copies)
